So how do we load a non-default version of a software package? In this case, the
only change we need to make is be more specific about the module we are loading
by leaving in the version number after the `/`.

```
{{ site.remote.prompt }} module load gromacs/2023.3
{{ site.remote.prompt }} gmx
```
{: .bash}

```

The following have been reloaded with a version change:
  1) gromacs/2024.4 => gromacs/2023.3

```
{: .output}

We now have successfully switched from GROMACS 2024.4 to GROMACS 2023.3. We are 
notified of the version change, and it appears that no dependencies required 
version changes.
